Rewritten: the two tools the provider gives a model, fact_store (add,
search, list, history, change, end, forget, stats) and fact_feedback
(helpful, unhelpful, confirmed); the recall before a turn, which searches
the turn's own message and puts the facts it recalls into that request; the
fact itself - one standalone sentence with the keywords someone would ask
for it by, a trust score, an origin and the dates it held; the versions a
change and an end keep; and the file it all lives in. The rewrite is Common
Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract, so the SQLite database became one
file of Lisp data written atomically beside the old one, and the tools and
the command are Nodecode's own.

Left out, because the rewrite is a fraction of the provider's size: the HRR
(holographic reduced representation) vectors and the dual-view cosine that
re-ranks candidates by meaning, so recall here is by words and word forms
only; the optional online stages (an embeddings API for search by meaning, a
cross-encoder for rescoring) and every switch that configures them; the
entity index (probe, reason, alias, rename, split, delete_entity) and the
merge verb; the multilingual stemmers and dictionaries; the review, enrich
and export verbs; the opt-in experience journal (fact_experience); auto
extraction of preferences from a conversation; and the per-user, per-chat
and per-thread scopes, so one store serves this home.
